<ServiceLayout
  serviceName="Gas Fitting"
  serviceSlug="gas-fitting"
  heroTitle="Licensed Gas Fitting Services Across South-East Queensland"
  heroSubtitle="Gas line installation, appliance connections, leak repairs and safety inspections — by QBCC-licensed gas fitters serving residential and commercial clients across Brisbane, Logan, Gold Coast and Ipswich."
  keyBenefits={[
    'Licensed gas fitters — QBCC licence and licensed to work on Type A and Type B appliances',
    '24/7 emergency response for gas leaks — call us and we respond immediately',
    'Full compliance: gas compliance certificates issued for all regulated work',
    'Expertise across natural gas and LPG systems, both residential and commercial',
  ]}
  process={[
    {
      title: 'Safety first',
      description: 'All gas work begins with a safety assessment. For suspected leaks, we attend as an emergency — isolating the supply and ventilating before any diagnosis.',
    },
    {
      title: 'Scope and quote',
      description: 'We assess the work required — new installation, connection, repair or appliance replacement — and provide a clear, upfront quote before any work begins.',
    },
    {
      title: 'Complete the work',
      description: 'All gas work is completed by a licensed gas fitter in accordance with AS/NZS 5601 and Queensland regulations. We use quality materials rated for the applicable pressure class.',
    },
    {
      title: 'Test and certify',
      description: 'We perform a pressure test on all completed work and issue a Certificate of Compliance for all regulated gas installations, which you keep for insurance and resale purposes.',
    },
  ]}
  faqs={[
    {
      q: 'What should I do if I smell gas?',
      a: 'If you smell gas: do not turn on or off any electrical switches or appliances, do not use a phone inside the building, extinguish any naked flames, open windows and doors, and leave the building immediately. From a safe distance, call 000 if you suspect a major leak, then call us on 0452 188 420. We provide 24/7 emergency gas response.',
    },
    {
      q: 'What gas work requires a licensed gas fitter?',
      a: 'In Queensland, all gas work on fixed gas installations must be carried out by a licensed gas fitter. This includes installing or modifying gas lines, connecting gas appliances to a fixed supply, repairing gas leaks, replacing gas meters or regulators, and installing gas hot water systems or cooktops.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Do you issue gas compliance certificates?',
      a: 'Yes. A Certificate of Compliance is issued for all regulated gas work and is required under Queensland legislation. This certificate is important for insurance purposes, property transactions and body corporate records.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Can you connect a new gas appliance, BBQ point or outdoor kitchen?',
      a: 'Yes. We install dedicated gas points for BBQs, outdoor kitchens, pool heaters, patio heaters and commercial cooking equipment. All connections are tested and certified.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Do you work on LPG as well as natural gas?',
      a: 'Yes. We service both natural gas (reticulated mains) and LPG (bottled or bulk) systems for residential and commercial applications.',
    },
    {
      q: 'What areas do you cover for gas fitting services?',
      a: 'We service Brisbane (south), Logan City, Redland City, Gold Coast (north) and Ipswich — more than 130 suburbs within 30 km of Loganholme.',
    },
  ]}
